Subject: [PATCH] rtl8xxxu: keep the beacon queued in AP mode

With bit 3 of REG_MBID_NUM clear, the chip clears the beacon queue after
each beacon it sends: one beacon goes out after every beacon update and
then none until the next one. Stations find the AP through probe
responses, but once associated they get no beacons and leave after ~2 s
(deauth reason 4, "inactivity"). Seen on the RTL8188EU of a MOD Duo: the
TBDOK bit of REG_HISR0 was never set while BCNDMAINT0 was set at every
TBTT.

Set bits 3 and 4 of REG_MBID_NUM when the AP interface is added, as the
vendor driver (r8188eu, rtw_set_opmode) does.

Applies on top of 0006.
---
--- a/rtl8xxxu_core.c
+++ b/rtl8xxxu_core.c
@@ -6690,6 +6690,15 @@
 		rtl8xxxu_write16(priv, REG_TSFTR_SYN_OFFSET, 0x7fff); /* ~32ms */
 		rtl8xxxu_write8(priv, REG_DUAL_TSF_RST, DUAL_TSF_RESET_TSF0);
 
+		/*
+		 * With bit 3 clear the chip drops the beacon from its queue
+		 * after sending it, and sends no more beacons until the next
+		 * update (the vendor driver sets bits 3 and 4).
+		 */
+		val8 = rtl8xxxu_read8(priv, REG_MBID_NUM);
+		val8 |= BIT(3) | BIT(4);
+		rtl8xxxu_write8(priv, REG_MBID_NUM, val8);
+
 		/* enable BCN0 function */
 		rtl8xxxu_write8(priv, REG_BEACON_CTRL,
 				BEACON_DISABLE_TSF_UPDATE |
